            <title>[LU-21191] sanity-sec test_21: cannot chmod mapped_trusted_noadmin, MDT export stays on default nodemap (SSK)</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21191</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity-sec test_21 (mapped_trusted_noadmin) fails intermittently with&lt;br/&gt;
"cannot chmod mapped_trusted_noadmin:60000:c0:0:003" on code that already&lt;br/&gt;
contains the &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19157" title="Ban clients from nodemap" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19157"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19157&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; fixes (change 69458, "do not apply ban list on the&lt;br/&gt;
MGS", merged 2026-11-06). Failures continue after the merge: two&lt;br/&gt;
lustre-master-next sessions on 2026-11-09 (full-dne-ipv6-part-2) and four&lt;br/&gt;
review sessions on 2026-11-11 (review-dne-selinux-ssk-part-2), from&lt;br/&gt;
unrelated changes (patchsets 6, 12, 12 and 68627 ps19). Before the merge&lt;br/&gt;
the same error was linked to &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19157" title="Ban clients from nodemap" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19157"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19157&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (15 failures, first seen 2026-09-30).&lt;br/&gt;
Rate on review runs is about 0.3% for the SSK group.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Failed subtest: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/sub_tests/24359028-a659-45d4-9f42-36358f8a4c13" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/sub_tests/24359028-a659-45d4-9f42-36358f8a4c13&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Session: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/c8963db7-1a9f-448f-9628-3a01b1b4705d" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/c8963db7-1a9f-448f-9628-3a01b1b4705d&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What the log shows: after nodemap_modify c0 admin=1 trusted=1 (synced on&lt;br/&gt;
MGS and servers), the root client of c0 gets EPERM from&lt;br/&gt;
"lfs setdirstripe -c 1 -i 1 /mnt/lustre/d21.sanity-sec" (MDT0001), so the&lt;br/&gt;
later chmod finds no directory. The remote MDTs (MDT0001, MDT0003) log&lt;br/&gt;
repeatedly during the test:&lt;br/&gt;
  nm_member_reclassify_nodemap() lustre-MDT0001: not reclassifying&lt;br/&gt;
  10.240.46.53@tcp to nodemap c0, inconsistent with nodemap default used&lt;br/&gt;
  in authentication: rc = -1&lt;br/&gt;
so the client export stays on the default nodemap (admin=0, root&lt;br/&gt;
squashed) instead of c0. No ban message is logged, so this is not the&lt;br/&gt;
banlist path 69458 fixed; it looks like the export keeps the nodemap it&lt;br/&gt;
authenticated with (SSK, from &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19079" title="gss for nodemap identification" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19079"&gt;LU-19079&lt;/a&gt; gss_id handling) across nodemap&lt;br/&gt;
property/membership changes. &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19157" title="Ban clients from nodemap" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19157"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19157&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; itself (revoke export locks on&lt;br/&gt;
nodemap change) was suspected of the original test_21 regression by&lt;br/&gt;
Andreas on 2025-09-28.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The patch under test on this run (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20689" title="utils: support decimal (SI) size units" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20689"&gt;LU-20689&lt;/a&gt;, llapi size units) does not&lt;br/&gt;
touch nodemap code.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-68627-ps19-2cb0b8ea6a96 on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/68627" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/68627&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
